Explain why stainless steels, alloy steels, and cast irons need distinct processing evidence (@metal-stainless-cast-irons: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F", #source "../sources/Steels-Structure-Properties-and-Design.lingua#r_5CB9R75MR8424M7VJ5Y33FY0QF", #source "../sources/Smitheries-and-Foundries-BREF.lingua#r_7ZJ5479WTSPDER11K364F6T041", #source "../sources/Ironmaking-and-Steelmaking-NPTEL.lingua#r_0XJNFP35VJ24ZR6AZJ78EY03G0", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Bauxite-alumina-solution-circuits-and-residue.lingua#r_5GGD4Q68DT33WZQVNFZVY7MP36") { r_24G8BGM2R0SY1EYFR56E5GF4X9
**Read:** [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), the complete ferrous-alloy, cast-iron, stainless, and advanced steel material; [Steels: Structure, Properties, and Design — Bhadeshia and Honeycombe](../sources/Steels-Structure-Properties-and-Design.lingua#r_5CB9R75MR8424M7VJ5Y33FY0QF), whole applicable chapters and original references, when available; [Smitheries and Foundries Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Smitheries-and-Foundries-BREF.lingua#r_7ZJ5479WTSPDER11K364F6T041), the complete relevant cast-iron production/quality case; [Ironmaking and Steelmaking — Gour Gopal Roy, NPTEL](../sources/Ironmaking-and-Steelmaking-NPTEL.lingua#r_0XJNFP35VJ24ZR6AZJ78EY03G0), the full stainless/secondary-treatment context.

Ferrous materials span different compositions, phases, transformation behavior, solidification modes, and service needs. Stainless behavior depends on alloy chemistry, structure, surface/environment, and processing; a grade name does not prove corrosion resistance in every condition. Cast irons require their own graphite/carbide and matrix/solidification account rather than being treated as impure steel.

Compare alloy additions and impurity control, oxidation/reduction selectivity, gas behavior, heat treatment, solidification, and deformation/joining requirements. Preserving a valuable alloy element during refining can conflict with another chemical duty. The same bulk composition can produce different useful states after different thermal/deformation histories.

Use actual composition/structure/property and manufacturing evidence, with the applicable designation/specification and test basis. A micrograph label or nominal alloying percentage is a starting clue; phase identity, population, orientation, segregation, and defects still need independent observation.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete stainless/alloy-steel case and a cast-iron case from feed through qualified product. Derive one consequential chemical/phase balance and one process-structure relation for each. Compare a plausible alternative route/state, test against measured observations, and explain a failure or discrepancy. Later transformation, casting, heat-treatment, and performance sections provide the common quantitative tools needed to deepen both cases.

**Continue:** [Follow alumina production through mineral chemistry, circulating solution, and residue](Bauxite-alumina-solution-circuits-and-residue.lingua#r_5GGD4Q68DT33WZQVNFZVY7MP36).

